    "message": "⚠️ Known issue (date handling)\n\nWhen a datetime value containing timezone information is provided, the package may convert the date to the previous day due to local timezone conversion.\n\nExample:\n`\"2026-03-31T00:00:00.000Z\"` may be interpreted as `\"2026-03-30\"`.\n\n*Workaround*\nSend dates without time or timezone (format: `yyyy-MM-dd`).\n\n*Fix*\nThis issue has been fixed starting from version *20260316.+*\n",
    "reasons": [
      "CriticalBugs"
    ]
  },
